Here is an example of how a table of contents (TOC) can be generated automatically in a LaTeX document using the `tocloft` package:

1. First, add the following lines to the preamble of your LaTeX document to load the `tocloft` package:

```latex
\documentclass{article}

\usepackage{tocloft}

% Set the style of the TOC
\renewcommand{\cfttoctitlefont}{\hfill\Large\bfseries}
\renewcommand{\cftaftertoctitle}{\hfill}
\renewcommand{\cfttocpagestyle}{plain}

% Set the style of the section entries
\renewcommand{\cftsecfont}{\large\bfseries}
\renewcommand{\cftsecpagefont}{\large}

% Set the number of digits for the page numbers
\setcounter{tocdepth}{2} % Show section and subsection entries only

\begin{document}
```

2. In your document, use the `section` and `subsection` commands to create headings and add content:

```latex
